1. sastrawijs-ts
   License: MIT
   Homepage: https://github.com/mlengse/sastrawijs-ts
   npm: sastrawijs-ts
   Used for: Indonesian word stemming (Nazief-Adriani algorithm) in the
   default `id` pipeline.

   Provenance note (research R4): the Sastrawi root-word dictionary is
   derived from the kateglo.com word list, which is published under
   CC BY-NC-SA 3.0 (non-commercial). The package itself is distributed under
   the MIT license. If non-commercial terms are incompatible with a given
   redistribution, the `stem()` contract is engine-agnostic and the root-word
   list can be swapped behind the unchanged API (documented in README,
   "Upstream capabilities").

   Fork provenance note (FR-023): the adopted upstream is the user's fork
   https://github.com/mlengse/sastrawijs-ts, published to the npm registry as
   `sastrawijs-ts` (unscoped; the maintainer owns the name). The repository was
   renamed from `sastrawijs` and the old URL redirects. This replaces the
   original `sastrawijs@1.1.0` from github.com/damzaky/sastrawijs; stem output
   is byte-identical across the 67-word golden list.

2. hyphenasi
   License: ISC
   Homepage: https://github.com/mlengse/hyphenasi
   npm: hyphenasi
   Used for: hyphenation pattern lookups (`id`, `en`) driving the soft-hyphen
   line-breaking feature and the English syllable engine. Indonesian and
   English patterns are sourced from the hyphenation pattern archive
   distributed with this package.

   Fork provenance note (FR-023): the adopted upstream is the user's fork
   https://github.com/mlengse/hyphenasi, a fork of
   https://github.com/ytiurin/hyphen published to the npm registry as
   `hyphenasi` (unscoped; the maintainer owns the name). The repository was
   renamed from `hyphen` and the old URL redirects. This replaces the upstream
   `hyphen@1.14.1`; the fork's KBBI-derived Indonesian patterns are more
   accurate against the project's PUEBI golden list.

